Modifications: the files were modified. SKILL.md was written fresh in the
house style from both sources; the references were condensed and split into
interop.md, signals.md and project-and-build.md. Facts were rechecked against
the Godot 4.7 documentation (cross-language scripting, C# signals, C# basics
and platform support, the 4.4-to-4.5 and 4.6-to-4.7 migration guides). Fixes
on port: the .NET version is read from the project's .csproj and the
Godot.NET.Sdk version follows the editor instead of a 4.3.0 pin; GDScript
accesses C# members by their C# names (not snake_case); a stored lambda uses
the generated delegate type (an Action<T> field does not compile against a
generated [Signal] event); Connect with Callable.From is documented as
auto-disconnecting for custom signals; [GlobalClass] goes on a Node or
Resource subclass; the C# web export limitation, the Android .NET 9
requirement and the verified 4.7 C# breaking changes were added; the
unverified EnableGodotDotNetPreview property, the "namespace must match" rule,
the ConnectOnce helper and the C#-versus-GDScript speed table were dropped;
pointers to the godot-mcp editor addon's create_dotnet_project and
build_dotnet tools and to the csharp, msbuild and dotnet-testing plugins were
added.
